1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
*music*

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
*music*

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Well, that's intense.

4
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
*laughter*

5
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Good morning.

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
I welcome you all to the beginning of our series on Revelation.

7
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
We hope it's a revelation to you.

8
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
We hope you get at least three things out of this series that's gonna last through the summer.

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
As we invite you to read Revelation anew, like you've never read it before.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Just pick it up and really read it.

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
We hope you get a renewed perspective on this book, okay?

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
If you've looked at this book in the past with confusion, which is likely,

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
or with fear or with discontent over how it's played out around you previously,

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,000
my message to you is that this is a book of promise, okay?

15
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
As Jesus said in John's Gospel when he was talking about the judgment,

16
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
John 16:33, "I've told you these things so that in me you may have peace.

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
In this world you will have tribulation, but take heart, I have overcome the world."

18
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
That's all of Revelation right there.

19
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
He could have just said that.

20
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
This was a letter written to people going through tribulation.

21
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
They were being martyred.

22
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
They were going through all sorts of persecution.

23
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
They'd been told the Prince of Peace had come and the kingdom would be born and they'd be a part of it.

24
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
And now they're going through all this tribulation and Jesus has told them,

25
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
"You will have tribulation, but take heart.

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
At the end, righteousness prevails and I will overcome the evil of the world."

27
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
That's the story of Revelation.

28
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
So we hope you get that renewed perspective and then you can see that when you read it.

29
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
The second thing is a renewed insight.

30
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Renewed insight is going to come, unfortunately, by you putting in a little work, right?

31
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
That's the way that always works.

32
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:39,000
And what we need you to do is not much work, but it's going to require a careful reading of the text from everybody here, okay?

33
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:51,000
If you've avoided reading this for years because you've just heard it once too often, or you've heard too many crazy things about it, or you tried to read it once and it seemed a little bizarre,

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:57,000
or the people you knew just were a little too intense about it so you backed off, or you may be one of the people who've read it.

35
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,000
You have a distinct and thorough explanation for everything in it and you don't think you need to read it anymore, right?

36
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:06,000
If any of that is you, we want you to read it again from scratch, okay?

37
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:14,000
And this week, what I need you to do is hear it the way the early church heard it, which is all at once, out loud, without chapter breaks, okay?

38
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:23,000
So, get with your spouse or a significant other or your friend and one of you read it to the other person and if you don't have somebody, which is fine, your phone will do it for you, right?

39
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:28,000
You can log into the Bible app and it will read Revelation to you all at once on your way to work, okay?

40
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:40,000
And we need you to read it that way because the early church never had the education opportunity or resources to go through and parse it word by word and look up what every image meant and it just didn't happen.

41
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:45,000
They sat in church and somebody read the whole thing out to them at once and it just washed over them, all these images.

42
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
And it was a big picture.

43
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
So, we want everyone to do that this week, okay?

44
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Read it out loud.

45
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
You can read it out loud to yourself, that's also okay.

46
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
But get your phone, have someone read it to you, you read it to them.

47
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:01,000
And then as we go through the summer, it'll be 22 chapters over 10 weeks.

48
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
So, you know, roughly two chapters a week, you can read more slowly along with us.

49
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,000
But we want you to get that first impulse, impact this week.

50
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Yes, sir.

51
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Why out loud?

52
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Why out loud?

53
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Because that's how the early church would have read it.

54
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
I just want you to hear it the way they heard it.

55
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Also, when you read it out loud, your ears hear what your mouth is saying and it goes in twice.

56
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Yeah.

57
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:34,000
So, the last thing is, so a renewed perspective and insight, but also a renewed mission.

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:43,000
In verse 4 of Revelation, actually verse 3, he says, "Blessed is the one who reads aloud the words of the prophecy."

59
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
That's another reason to read it out loud, right?

60
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
"Blessed is the one who reads aloud the words of the prophecy."

61
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,000
"Blessed are those who hear it and keep what's written in it for the time is near."

62
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
So, that "keep what's written in it."

63
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Some translations you have will say, "Keep it, heed it, obey it, take to heart."

64
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
That's one of them.

65
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
"Obey it."

66
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
This is the Hebrew concept of Shema, right?

67
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
"To hear and to obey."

68
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
You haven't really heard it until you've obeyed it.

69
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:14,000
You'll notice when you read Revelation, the direct commands are at a minimum.

70
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:18,000
So, you might ask yourself, "How can I heed and obey this that I'm hearing?"

71
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
The answer is, that's your job this summer is to answer that question, okay?

72
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
I'm on the schedule to speak the last week.

73
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:30,000
And when I get up here, I'm going to ask, "How do you keep and heed the words of this prophecy?"

74
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Right?

75
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
That's the thing we have to decide this summer.

76
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
You need to read this book and don't say, "What does it mean?

77
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
What does it mean I should do?"

78
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Right?

79
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:45,000
We sang this morning, "Standing on the solid rock, you've seen me through the storms."

80
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Jesus, that parable is in Matthew 25.

81
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:55,000
He says, "Everyone who hears these words of mine and acts on them, and acts on them, will be like a wise man who builds his house on the rock.

82
00:05:55,000 --> 00:06:01,000
And the rains fell, and the floods came, and the winds blew and slammed against the house, and yet it didn't fall because it was founded on the rock."

83
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:08,000
In Luke, where he prefaces that with the sentence, "Why do you call me Lord, Lord, when you don't do what I tell you?"

84
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Right?

85
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Why are you saying, "I'm your Lord, I'm your leader, I'm the one to who you have fealty," when you're not doing it?

86
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,000
I'm trying to give you a solid rock on which to build your house, right?

87
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:26,000
So, when it says, "He who hears and reads the words of this prophecy and keeps them, obeys them," there's something that we're supposed to do.

88
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
This is a book that should lead us to action.

89
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
We've got 10 weeks to figure out what that action is.

90
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,000
All right?

91
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Thank you.

92
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Thank you.

93
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
That's good.

94
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:44,000
So, the book opens with, as we sequence that action, the book opens with the revelation of Jesus Christ.

95
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,000
So, the focus is on Jesus.

96
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
As we go through the summer, it's important to keep that in mind.

97
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
This is a revelation of Jesus.

98
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
It's not a revelation of what?

99
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Armageddon, the beast, the four horsemen.

100
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
It's not a revelation of the bowls of wrath.

101
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:07,000
It's not the rapture or the antichrist, right?

102
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
And, incidentally, rapture and antichrist, two words never used in Revelation.

103
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
So, it's definitely not a revelation of those two things, right?

104
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Most importantly, though, it's not a revelation of you.

105
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
It's not a revelation of me.

106
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
It's not a revelation of what's going to happen to me.

107
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
It's a revelation of Jesus.

108
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
He's told us there's going to be tribulation.

109
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
There's a picture of some tribulation that the people are going through.

110
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:32,000
But the revelation is, at the end of it, Christ reigns.

111
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
That's the revelation.

112
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
So, it's a revelation of Christ.

113
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
And we see images of Christ over and over.

114
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
So, we don't want to look for ourselves.

115
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
We want to look for Christ.

116
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
And that can be confusing because of all the images.

117
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
But I want to give you guys a visual picture.

118
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:49,000
And to understand this, you have to understand that I grew up in Alabama, where there is only

119
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
football.

120
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Oh, my goodness.

121
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
I'm an Auburn fan.

122
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,000
But that's exactly it.

123
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Growing up in Alabama, there is several million people with a misplaced pathology focused on

124
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
a single game, right?

125
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
That dominates our 365 days a year.

126
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:15,000
And every conversation I have with somebody, I'm aware of what tribe they're in.

127
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Fortunes and marriages and businesses and friendships are born and lost over this game.

128
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
And it dominates everything.

129
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:27,000
I grew up an Auburn fan, but I grew up in the shadow of Legion Field, which was where Alabama

130
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
played half their games.

131
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
It was a big giant stadium in Birmingham.

132
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:37,000
And I sold programs at all the Alabama games to my arch enemy, you know, so that I could

133
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
be a lead seller, so that I could get in to sell programs at the Iron Bowl once a year.

134
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Because that was the only way I could get a ticket, and I could never afford one anyway.

135
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,000
And that didn't even give me a seat.

136
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
It just allowed me to get in the stadium.

137
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
I'd get there two hours early to the Iron Bowl.

138
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
If I was a top seller, I could sell at the Iron Bowl.

139
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
I'd get there early, sell several boxes.

140
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
And that would allow me to walk around during the game half-heartedly holding a program

141
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
in the air while I watched the game, right?

142
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:12,000
And it's impossible to explain to you the intensity of the emotion of 100,000 people focused on

143
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
that one day of the year, right?

144
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:20,000
And when I would come out from under the darkness of the stands holding my box of programs, just

145
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:24,000
a noise like a thousand waterfalls behind me would come over, and the Alabama band, the

146
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:28,000
million dollar band's coming up, and the mockery of the Auburn band, you know, is coming back

147
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
at them, and the Simpson Peppers yelling over the loudspeaker.

148
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
It was this enormous event.

149
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:38,000
And I would hear behind me this guy with the most inventive stream of abuse, right, aimed

150
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
at the other side.

151
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
And I would hear it, and I would turn.

152
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
And if I say to you, I saw this thing, and it was amazing, and then I heard, and I turned,

153
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
and I saw what he was doing, it would sound to you like he just did that.

154
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
But I assure you, he'd been going for hours, right?

155
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
And he is going to continue hurling the statements for the rest of this several hours.

156
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:58,000
But I'm telling you to give you a picture of what I'm seeing, what I observed in the order

157
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
I observed it.

158
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:04,000
All these things are happening concurrently and consecutively and in repetition.

159
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
The popcorn guy is yelling popcorn over and over.

160
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
This guy behind me yelling abuse will not stop, right?

161
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,000
It's going to go for the whole game.

162
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:18,000
And I tell you what I saw when it's relevant to draw the picture for you of what I experienced

163
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
that day.

164
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:23,000
In this massive stadium with hundreds of thousands of people doing their own thing, but each one

165
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
focused on what's happening at the center.

166
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:31,000
As the ref makes a call, the ball moves, everyone stops and looks in wonder at this one thing,

167
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:36,000
and then they go back to their various activities, extolling the wonders of this game.

168
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
This is clearly what John's going through, except that when I tell you this, you guys have seen

169
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
a football game.

170
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,000
You've been to a stadium.

171
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
You have context for this.

172
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
I can use words that you understand.

173
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:51,000
John was thrust into a heavenly realm, and he just had to see everything in all of heaven.

174
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:55,000
An angel came and lifted the veil and showed him what was under there, and he's scribbling

175
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:58,000
madly with a pen to try to say, "I saw this, and then I saw this, and then I saw this,

176
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:03,000
and then I saw this," and if we were to take that as some sort of simple linear story, we

177
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
would miss what he's telling us.

178
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:09,000
He's telling us, as he turns around and hears a voice and turns and sees and turns and sees

179
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:13,000
what's happening in all of heaven, and he's got to go back and repeat himself, because

180
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:20,000
it's impossible to convey in human language something for which we have no context.

181
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:28,000
So this revelation of Jesus, we see him as a picture.

182
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:32,000
We see him pictured as a conquering king with a sword coming out of his mouth ready to meet

183
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
out justice.

184
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
We see him as a slain lamb, a young baby.

185
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
We see him as an indomitable king.

186
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
We see him as an eternal God who overcame death.

187
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Many images, but each of those images is trying to convey something to us about his character

188
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,000
at that moment and his significance at that moment.

189
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Think of the last time you had an argument with your wife or significant other.

190
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:56,000
It takes like two minutes, but the nuance of every letter has meaning.

191
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
And there's a huge back story behind everything you say.

192
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:05,000
And for Dave to explain to me that little two-minute conversation would take 40 pages of writing

193
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
to really thoroughly explain to me every nuance and every meaning of everything.

194
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:13,000
And that's something he knows completely about, and he could never convey it all to me.

195
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:17,000
John is trying to convey this enormous experience for which we have no context.

196
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:23,000
And he's got to use some sort of image or metaphor, something that uses the language we have

197
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,000
to convey something that we can't conceive.

198
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:33,000
So he gives us images over and over of Christ as the slain lamb and a young baby and a conquering king.

199
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
The first image we have is in Revelation chapter one.

200
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,000
I'm going to start in verse nine, where he says,

201
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,000
"I, John, your brother and partner in the tribulation and the kingdom

202
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
and the patient endurance that are in Jesus, was on the island of Patmos

203
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
on account of the word of God and the testimony of Jesus."

204
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
That means he's in a penal colony because he wouldn't stop preaching, okay?

205
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:57,000
John worked with some churches in Western, what's today, Western Turkey.

206
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:01,000
He called it Asia. We call it Asia Minor today, but it's Turkey.

207
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
And there were a number of churches there.

208
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:09,000
And he wouldn't stop preaching the seditious message of a different ruler, a different Prince of Peace,

209
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
a different Son of God than Rome recognized in their cult of the emperor.

210
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
And so he was sent to a penal colony, which today, it's just right off the coast.

211
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,000
But without modern communication and conveyance, he must have been on the other end of the world.

212
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
You know, he might as well have been.

213
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
So he's on the island called Patmos on account of preaching.

214
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,000
I was in the spirit on the Lord's day, so he's worshiping.

215
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
And I heard behind me the voice like a trumpet saying, "Write what you see in a book and send it to the seven churches."

216
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:42,000
So seven churches that he works with: Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and Laodicea.

217
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
So he hears something, wants to know what it is, turns.

218
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Then I turned to see the voice that was speaking to me, and on turning, I saw seven golden lampstands.

219
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:57,000
And in the midst of the lampstands, one like the Son of Man, clothed with a long robe, golden sash around his chest.

220
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
The hairs of his head were white, like white wool, like snow.

221
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
His eyes were flaming fire.

222
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:06,000
His feet were burnished bronze refined in a furnace, so no dross, just glowing.

223
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
His voice was like the roar of many waters, like a trumpet and like the roar of many waters, just a massive sound.

224
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:18,000
In his right hand, he held seven stars, and out of his mouth came a sharp two-edged sword.

225
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:22,000
And his face was like the sun, shining in full strength."

226
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
This is a terrifying image, right?

227
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:28,000
John would be excused if he were frightened.

228
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:32,000
And in verse 17, "When I saw him, I fell at his feet as though dead."

229
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
He was frightened.

230
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:39,000
"But he lay his right hand on me, the hand of blessing, saying, 'Fear not, for I am the first and the last.'"

231
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:43,000
So this figure is now identifying himself as the Yahweh Creator God.

232
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:49,000
In verse 4, he's already said, "Peace to you from he who was and who is to come."

233
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:53,000
In verse 8, "The Alpha and Omega," says the Lord God, "who is and who was and who is to come."

234
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
This person is now identifying," and John set that up deliberately,

235
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
"identifying as the one who is and was and is to come, the Alpha and Omega."

236
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
So he's seeing God in the midst of seven lampstands.

237
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,000
The divine.

238
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
"So I am the first and the last and the living one.

239
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
I died and behold, I live forevermore.

240
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
I have the keys of death and Hades."

241
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Well, he's already set that up.

242
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
In verse 5, "Jesus Christ is the faithful witness, the firstborn of the dead."

243
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:22,000
So this character is both the Creator God divine, a glorified picture of Jesus Christ.

244
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
John's never seen him like this, right?

245
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Last time John saw Jesus, he'd raised from the dead and he was talking to him as a person.

246
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:35,000
And now he's this immensely glorified figure that he correlates directly with God Almighty.

247
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
So this is an amazing moment for John.

248
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:42,000
And Jesus standing in the midst of these lampstands says to John,

249
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:47,000
"Write therefore the things you've seen, those that are and those that are to take place after that."

250
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,000
So that tells us two things.

251
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:55,000
One, some of the stuff in Revelation that he writes about is happening while John's alive, right?

252
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
You're going to write down things that are happening now.

253
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,000
He said that also in verse 9.

254
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:03,000
"I'm your brother and partner in tribulation and in the kingdom in patient endurance."

255
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:08,000
So the tribulation that he's writing about, again, this is a letter written to people undergoing tribulation and persecution.

256
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
It's happening to John.

257
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
He's in a penal colony, right?

258
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
He's a partner in this.

259
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:22,000
So part of what's in Revelation, it's happening during his life in AD 65 to 95, somewhere back then, a long time ago.

260
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:26,000
And some of it are things that are to take place after this.

261
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
In verse 3, it tells us the time is near for those things.

262
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:36,000
So at some point, probably pretty soon after John experiences this, some of the events are going to happen.

263
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
It's possible some will be in the distant future.

264
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
So some is happening in his life.

265
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Some very soon.

266
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
It's possible some will be later.

267
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
So that we hear right away.

268
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Write these things down.

269
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:50,000
"As for the mystery of the seven stars that you saw in my right hand in verse 20, and the seven golden lampstands,

270
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:55,000
the seven stars are the angels of the seven churches, and the seven lampstands are the seven churches."

271
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Okay, no big mystery there, but it's significant.

272
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Notice he didn't explain why my hair is glowing, why I have flashing eyes and glowing feet, right?

273
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Because those were all images directly out of prophecy.

274
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:16,000
When John describes Jesus that way, he's pulling straight from Daniel chapter 7 and 10.

275
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:20,000
And the picture of the holiness of God is straight from Ezekiel's vision.

276
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
And the sword in the mouth is right out of Isaiah.

277
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:28,000
He's using pictures pulled from a prophecy that everyone reading this would have known cold.

278
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
And so they understand exactly what he means by it.

279
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,000
The seven lampstands and the seven angels, they didn't have an image for that.

280
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
So it had to be explained.

281
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:39,000
This tells us he expected them to understand what he's writing.

282
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,000
This wasn't mysterious.

283
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,000
It wasn't cryptic.

284
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
He was saying something in language that they understood.

285
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,000
And if they didn't understand it, he told them immediately, right?

286
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:53,000
So, the seven golden lampstands, that's an image out of Zechariah that's being reused.

287
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:57,000
In Zechariah, you guys know what a menorah is, right?

288
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,000
It's the seven-branched symbol of Hanukkah.

289
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,000
That was the lamp.

290
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:06,000
And the Hebrew word used here is menorah because that's the Hebrew word for this lamp.

291
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,000
And so it was a lamp with seven branches.

292
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,000
This is seven of those, seven sevens.

293
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,000
So this is an amplified holy, holy version of what Zechariah had experienced.

294
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:24,000
And the lamps, they served in the tabernacle and the temple to illuminate the way to the holy of holies, to get from man to God, right?

295
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:29,000
So here we have each of the seven churches serving to guide the way to Jesus standing in their midst.

296
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Jesus said, "Don't hide your lamp under a bushel.

297
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Put it on a lampstand for all to see so they can come to me."

298
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
And that's what they're seeing.

299
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
He's seeing a vision of these seven churches functioning as they should.

300
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,000
They're illuminating a path to Jesus who's in their midst.

301
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
He's standing there guiding them.

302
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
And each of the seven churches has an angel.

303
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
What's an angel?

304
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:51,000
It's a divine messenger is what angel literally means.

305
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
If an angel is sent from God, it's a messenger sent from God.

306
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:56,000
So he's in communication with these churches, right?

307
00:18:56,000 --> 00:19:01,000
So that image is there's seven churches leading people to me and I'm communicating with and guiding these churches.

308
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:07,000
And by the way, I am the creator God ready to judge the earth with the sword of righteousness in my mouth.

309
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,000
So I'm with them, right?

310
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Now the next time we see Jesus, he's going to be a baby.

311
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
And then a slain lamb.

312
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:18,000
And then all these other images until chapter 19, he's going to be this image again.

313
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Does that mean he's morphing back and forth?

314
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:24,000
That means that John is describing what his significance is in each of these pictures.

315
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
What he means to this moment, to this vision.

316
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:38,000
And right now, he is already the immense ruler of the world in all creation that he will be again in chapter 19.

317
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
He's letting you know he's already everything God will ever be.

318
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
He's unchangeable.

319
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Don't be fooled by the changing images.

320
00:19:46,000 --> 00:20:01,000
So each time we see an image of Christ, the image is going to be rendered and surrounded in a rich, complex tapestry of known visual language images that reference things that we don't readily understand today.

321
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:06,000
So this summer, it's our job to help you make sure everybody knows what those images are.

322
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Back then, the people who read it would have just known from their previous education.

323
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Because while this letter is written from John to the seven churches in modern-day Turkey that he references in chapter 4, it is also a prophecy, right?

324
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
He says this is a book of prophecy.

325
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
So it's a letter containing prophecy.

326
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:27,000
And I just want to recap with you guys real quickly from the Jonah series what prophecy is.

327
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
A prophet is not a crystal ball gazer who tells the future.

328
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
That is not a prophet.

329
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
A prophet is someone who declares the word of God that God gave him this.

330
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:39,000
And we're seeing at this moment how Jesus gave John this message.

331
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:48,000
He said in chapter, in verse 1, God gave it to Jesus who sent an angel to pull up the curtain and show it to John and tell him to write it down, right?

332
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
So that's what happened.

333
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:53,000
This is a letter of prophecy, which doesn't necessarily tell the future.

334
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Typically in prophecy, a prophet will say, if you disobey God, this will be the result.

335
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:02,000
If you're obedient to me, if you have fidelity to me, these will be the blessings.

336
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:07,000
So there's a possible future coming to you depending on how you behave is typically the word of a prophet.

337
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:10,000
It wouldn't be surprising if that's what happens in this book.

338
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,000
So when we're looking for what does this mean?

339
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,000
How do we keep the words of this book?

340
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,000
We should keep that in mind.

341
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Not only is it a prophetic text though, it also relies heavily on prophetic imagery and references to Old Testament prophecy.

342
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,000
But it's also an apocalyptic text.

343
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:32,000
And that makes it a little more complicated because apocalypse, and by the way, the name of this book is the apocalypsis.

344
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
That's the Greek word.

345
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
And it means unveiling, uncovering what was formerly unknown.

346
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
So there's a mystery.

347
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
And by mystery, we don't mean puzzle that can be deduced.

348
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,000
We mean thing you could never know unless somebody takes the cover off.

349
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
This is like Schrodinger's cat, right?

350
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Until you look, you don't know what's there ever, right?

351
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:52,000
So the mystery is revealed by an apocalypse.

352
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:58,000
It's also revealed, that's why the book is called Revelation, because that's a translation of the word apocalypse.

353
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:03,000
But an apocalyptic text is an imaginative form of literature that we don't use anymore.

354
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:11,000
When I say imaginative literature, you think of poems, screenplays, novels, all narratives, right?

355
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,000
With the possible exception of some poems, right?

356
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:15,000
But they're still telling you kind of a thing that happened to me.

357
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:24,000
The apocalypse is a set of images and a catalog of means of conveying, using word pictures,

358
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:28,000
the emotions and importance, significance of something that language can't convey.

359
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:32,000
Telling you something totally out of context, which is what John is doing here.

360
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:37,000
He's been thrust into the heavenly realm, has to tell us what he saw, and there's no words for those things.

361
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:43,000
So he uses the catalog of apocalyptic imagery to tell us what it means and what the significance is

362
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,000
and what's going to happen.

363
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:52,000
If we, it's very important then that we take the time to figure out how to read an apocalyptic text.

364
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Because it's not an image we use, a type of writing we use anymore.

365
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:02,000
It's used for revealing mystery, which standard language can't encapsulate.

366
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:07,000
And it describes what is unseen using images of what is seen.

367
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
So it has to use metaphors and images.

368
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:17,000
This text is a fourth thing, and that is that it borrows very heavily from Roman national cult of imperialism.

369
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:26,000
There's any number of parallels between the language used in Revelation and the language used in propaganda in support of the Roman government.

370
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:31,000
And that's more than we could go over today, but you should go back online and watch Dr. Silva's second session.

371
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
He had four lectures yesterday.

372
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:38,000
The second one covers that in a way that will blow some of your minds, but it will be very informative for everyone.

373
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:42,000
So we have to read this very carefully.

374
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:45,000
We have to read this book, I'd say cautiously.

375
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:48,000
And by cautiously, I don't mean slowly and with trepidation.

376
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,000
I mean eagerly, right?

377
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:53,000
You want to read every word, but you have to know what it says before you say what it means.

378
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:58,000
And you have to very eagerly read and know every word.

379
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:01,000
Don't substitute in concepts that you've heard.

380
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Don't speed past things that seem confusing.

381
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Read and know exactly what it says.

382
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:08,000
And then we slowly go back and say, what does it mean?

383
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:11,000
So we have to read it cautiously in that way.

384
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:14,000
If we don't have the language of the prophets in mind as we read Revelation,

385
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:16,000
we're just going to miss a lot of what John is telling us.

386
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:20,000
That's evident even in that first image, right, of Jesus.

387
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:23,000
If we're not familiar with the normal imagery of apocalyptic writing,

388
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:27,000
we're likely to explain those images using our current catalog of life and literature.

389
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:31,000
And that's going to be really misleading, because we don't use the images the same way anymore.

390
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:34,000
If we're unfamiliar with Roman imagery, we're just going to miss it.

391
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:38,000
We'll miss his snide takes on the propaganda of the time.

392
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:42,000
We'll miss what the immediate and clear meaning was to that first century audience.

393
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Which is, again, why you need to watch David De Silva's second session.

394
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:52,000
In either case, when we read, if we read it without caution,

395
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:58,000
we'll be attempting to provide a physical narrative explanation of images and actions that are emotive,

396
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:03,000
metaphoric, and symbolic, and usually not narrative, right?

397
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:06,000
So we need to be very cautious as we read it.

398
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Throughout the history of the church, many schools of interpretation have grown up,

399
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:13,000
as people have really dug in and tried to understand Revelation.

400
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:18,000
And what's important to understand is that there are multiple Orthodox schools of understanding this.

401
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:21,000
If you take any of the major Orthodox schools of interpretation,

402
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:27,000
there are significant, scholarly, respected, pious men who just came to different conclusions.

403
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:31,000
And it's based a lot on their experience in their life and where they're coming from.

404
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:34,000
We actually did a class for the last ten weeks.

405
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,000
If you were in that class, raise your hand.

406
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:39,000
We just want people around the audience to talk to them.

407
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:43,000
And we went through the major schools of understanding Revelation,

408
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:49,000
so that we could understand what we've heard and where it lies in the pantheon of different ideas.

409
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:55,000
There's four, the four basic schools are, one is that it mostly or all happened in the past,

410
00:25:55,000 --> 00:26:00,000
around the time that the temple was destroyed and Israel was invaded by Rome.

411
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:03,000
That was the persecution and the persecutions that surrounded that.

412
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:07,000
One school of thought says that the vast majority of Revelation refers to those events,

413
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:11,000
which would have been a prophecy from John, but an hour distant past, right?

414
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:14,000
The second school of thought is that it's kind of current.

415
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:18,000
It takes the full sweep of church history from that time to the distant future of judgment,

416
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,000
and that we're just in the middle of it, right?

417
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:24,000
And a third school of thought says that it's all in the future,

418
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:27,000
either in the very near or very distant future,

419
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:31,000
and that these events will play out in a way that's yet to be seen.

420
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:36,000
And incidentally, there's a recent, it started in the 1800s but got popular in the 1970s,

421
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:41,000
a recent version of the future understanding, which sees this all as very specific,

422
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:44,000
usually Israel-focused geopolitical conflict.

423
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:50,000
And that's the one we see in movies and novels and stuff that's gotten really popular.

424
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:54,000
But that's a very new understanding of what Revelation can mean, just as a side note.

425
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:56,000
And while there's a lot of people that talk about it today,

426
00:26:56,000 --> 00:27:00,000
historically it's unheard of among a lot of the church.

427
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:09,000
But the fourth major understanding of how Revelation works is that it's patterns, right?

428
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:14,000
There will always be persecution and Christ will always come and bring righteousness.

429
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:20,000
There will always be someone trying to replace God with current evil human systems.

430
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,000
And God will have to always prevail over that.

431
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:24,000
And if we stay faithful, we'll always be saved.

432
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,000
So that's sort of the fourth one.

433
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:30,000
So it's in the past, ongoing, in the present, in the future, or symbolic.

434
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:32,000
There are sort of the four ways of understanding it.

435
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:39,000
And again, wherever you fall, the main thing is to know that Jesus is at the center of all of those, right?

436
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:43,000
You can read it every way, and I encourage you to study.

437
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:46,000
I encourage you, after you've just read it through quickly and really gotten it in your head,

438
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,000
go back and study what people have said.

439
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:53,000
And you'll find there are authorities who, with great intent, really support each of those.

440
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:54,000
And that's not new.

441
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:58,000
We know that within a generation of Revelation being written,

442
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:01,000
the church leaders were already developing different schools.

